eved September 3, 2013.\n106. ↑ \"The Life and writings of Dr. Jose Rzal\". National Historical Commission of The Philippines. Archived from the original on September 16, 2013. Retrieved September 3, 2013.\n107. ↑ Marcelo H. del Pilar letter to José Rizal dated February 17, 1889, in Spanish, quoted in Norman G. Owens, \"Masculinity and national identity in 19th-century Philippines,\" *Illes i Imperis* 2 (1999), 40\n108. ↑ Morga, Antonio de (1890). *Sucesos de las Islas Filipinas*. Annotated by Rizal, José. Paris: Garnier Hermanos.\n109. ↑ \"The life and works of Jose Rizal\". Retrieved September 3, 2013.\n110. ↑ *The Reign of Greed by José Rizal*. Retrieved December 17, 2021.\n111. 1 2 Ocampo, Ambeth (February 25, 2005). \"Rizal's two unfinished novels\". *Looking Back*. Retrieved March 23, 2020.\n112. ↑ Rizal, José (1997). *Etikang Tagalog: Ang ikatlong nobela ni Rizal*. Lathalaing. ISBN 9719188707.\n113. ↑ Retana, W. E. (1907). *Vida y escritos del Dr. José Rizal* (in Spanish). Madrid: Librería General de Victoriano Suarez. p. 457. ISBN 978-5877689848. Retrieved March 23, 2020. `{{cite book}}`: ISBN / Date incompatibility (help)\n114. ↑ \"Himno Al Trabajo por José Rizal y Alonso\". *KapitBisig*. January 8, 2011.\n115. ↑ CCP Encyclopedia of Philippine Art, Vol 7., Cultural Center of the Philippines, 2015.\n116. ↑ Foreman, J., 1906, *The Philippine Islands, A Political, Geographical, Ethnographical, Social and Commercial History of the Philippine Archipelago*, New York: Charles Scribner's Sons\n117. ↑ Yoder, Robert L. \"The Life and of Dr. José Rizal\". Archived from the original on September 28, 2013.\n118. 1 2 \"New book reveals Rizal as master carver\". *Philippine Daily Inquirer*. March 22, 2021. Retrieved May 5, 2021.\n119. ↑ Ricardo Roque Pascual, *José Rizal Beyond the Grave* (Manila: P. Ayuda & Co., 1962)\n120. ↑ Ildefonso T. Runes and Mameto R. Buenafe, *The Forgery of the Rizal \"Retraction\" and Josephine's \"Autobiography\"* (Manila: BR Book Col, 1962).\n121. ↑ \"Rizal's Retraction: A Note on the Debate, Silliman Journal (Vol. 12, No. 2, April, May, June 1965), pages 168–183\". *Life and Writings of José Rizal*. Archived from the original on October 31, 2007. Retrieved September 9, 2009.\n122. ↑ Rafael Palma, Pride of the Malay Race (New York: Prentice Hall, 1949)\n123. 1 2 Ambeth Ocampo (2008). *Rizal Without the Overcoat*. Anvil Publishing.\n124. 1 2 3 Nicolas Zafra (1961). *Historicity of Rizal's Retraction*. Bookmark.\n125. ↑ Guerrero, León Maria III (1963). \"The First Filipino: A Biography of José Rizal\". National Historical Institute of The Philippines, Manila.\n126. 1 2 Gregorio Zaide (2003). *Jose Rizal: Life, Works and Writings of a Genius, Writer, Scientist and National Hero*. National Bookstore.\n127. ↑ Schumacher, John. \"The Making of a Nation: Essays on Nineteenth-Century Nationalism\".\n128. ↑ Molina, Antonio M. (1998). \"*Yo, José Rizal*\". Ediciones de Cultura Hispánica, Madrid.\n129. ↑ \"Uncovering Controversial Facts about José Rizal\" (mariaronabeltran.com)\n130. 1 2 3 Marciano Guzman (1988). *The Hard Facts About Rizal's Conversion*. Sinagtala Publishers. Archived from the original on July 8, 2011. Retrieved November 23, 2009.\n131. 1 2 Jesus Cavanna (1983). *Rizal's Unfading Glory: A Documentary History of the Conversion of Dr. Jose Rizal*.\n132. ↑ Javier de Pedro (2005) Rizal Through a Glass Darkly Archived December 31, 2010, at the Wayback Machine, University of Asia and the Pacific\n133. ↑ \"Evolution of Rizal's Religious Thought\" Archived January 15, 2010, at the Wayback Machine.\n134. ↑ (1950-01-06). \"Joint Statement of the Catholic Hierarchy of the Philippines on the Book 'The Pride of the Malay Race'\". CBCP (Catholic Bishop's Conference of the Philippines) Documents. Retrieved on September 30, 2012.\n135. ↑ Garcia, Ricardo P. (1964). \"*The Great Debate: The Rizal Retraction* – Preface\". R.P. Garcia Publishing Co., Quezon City.\n136. ↑ Esteban de Ocampo, *Why is Rizal the Greatest